; open-textbook.org — CAA records only.
;
; Import this rather than the whole zone file: `open-textbook.org.zone` also
; carries the `www` record, SPF and DMARC, which are already in the zone, and a
; re-import of those is at best a no-op and at worst a duplicate.
;
; Dashboard: DNS → Records → Import and Export → Import DNS records.
;
; CAA restricts which certificate authorities may issue for this domain. The
; issuer of the live certificate was checked first, because the failure mode is
; delayed: a list that omits the CA Cloudflare actually uses breaks nothing today
; and then fails to RENEW weeks later.
;
; Checked 2026-10-11 — the live certificate is issued by Google Trust Services
; (C=US, O=Google Trust Services, CN=WE1), valid to 2027-01-09. The three CAs
; below are the ones Cloudflare documents for custom domains, so this is a
; superset of what is known to be in use rather than a guess. Re-check it when
; that certificate comes up for renewal.
;
; The `pki.goog` parameter must stay inside the quotes: a semicolon outside
; quotes starts a BIND comment, and the parameter would be silently dropped.

open-textbook.org.  300  IN  CAA  0 issue      "letsencrypt.org"
open-textbook.org.  300  IN  CAA  0 issue      "pki.goog; cansignhttpexchanges=yes"
open-textbook.org.  300  IN  CAA  0 issue      "ssl.com"
open-textbook.org.  300  IN  CAA  0 issuewild   "letsencrypt.org"
open-textbook.org.  300  IN  CAA  0 issuewild   "pki.goog; cansignhttpexchanges=yes"
open-textbook.org.  300  IN  CAA  0 issuewild   "ssl.com"
